<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Fast DDS participant profile for EVERY participant of the f1tenth stack
  (fix batch 5, backlog H1). Loaded through FASTRTPS_DEFAULT_PROFILES_FILE,
  which is set by:
    - supervisor_bringup.launch.py and stack_bringup.launch.py, for the
      Discovery Server, the supervisor and every component (they inherit it);
    - scripts/env/jazzy.sh, for everything started by hand (ros2 / ros2cli,
      rosbag, scripts, the simulator on the sim host).

  What it changes: the participant lease. Every participant announces a 5 s
  lease (Fast DDS default 20 s) and re-announces itself every 1 s (default
  3 s). A participant that disappears without disposing (killed, or
  interrupted mid-shutdown) is dropped by the Discovery Server and by its
  peers within 5 s instead of 20 s.

  Why: a stack started while dead participants of the previous session were
  still registered intermittently failed to match some endpoints (slam_toolbox
  never activated, subscriptions never matched): 8 of 30 bringups with the
  default lease, 0 of 30 with this one (output/fix_batch_4_report.md, B3).

  Trade-off: a LIVE participant is dropped by mistake only if nothing from it
  arrives for 5 s, i.e. about 4 announcements in a row are not sent (its
  Fast DDS event thread starved) or lost. Measured under load in
  output/fix_batch_5_report.md.

  Nothing else: discovery protocol and server address still come from
  ROS_DISCOVERY_SERVER / ROS_SUPER_CLIENT, transports stay at the defaults.
  The lease is announced by each participant and enforced by whoever
  receives it, so a participant without this profile still works; it is only
  dropped after 20 s when it dies. The XML format is the same for Fast DDS
  2.6 (Humble) and 2.14 (Jazzy).

  No double hyphen anywhere inside this comment: it is illegal in an XML
  comment (see CLAUDE.md, Packaging).
-->
<profiles xmlns="http://www.eprosima.com/XMLSchemas/fastRTPS_Profiles">
  <participant profile_name="f1tenth_stack" is_default_profile="true">
    <rtps>
      <builtin>
        <discovery_config>
          <leaseDuration><sec>5</sec></leaseDuration>
          <leaseAnnouncement><sec>1</sec></leaseAnnouncement>
        </discovery_config>
      </builtin>
    </rtps>
  </participant>
</profiles>
